just in the last few moments this jury  of seven women and five men have reached  a verdict they've found el shafielshake  guilty on all eight charges of which he  was accused they found him guilty of  conspiracy to commit hostage-taking  resulting in the death of four american  citizens two journalists james foley and  stephen sotloff and aid workers kayla  mueller and peter kassig they've also  found him guilty of two wider charges of  which he was accused conspiracy to  provide material support to terrorists  and conspiracy to provide material  support to a designated foreign terror  organization that means that this jury  believes they've heard enough evidence  they've heard enough witness testimony  to believe that el shafiel sheikh was a  member of the so-called isis beatles  that group of british men who traveled  from london to syria to commit these  awful acts of holding 26 western  hostages including the british aid  workers alan henning and david haynes  before murdering them they believe that  al shafiel sheikh while not possibly  involved in the direct murder of these  individuals was certainly involved in  the hostage taking which led to their  killing  the families of those four american  individuals were in court all of them  were crying at the moment that that  verdict was read out the daughter of  british aid workers scottish aid worker  david haynes who went to syria to help  the plight of individuals there she was  crying incredibly loudly as that verdict  was read out those families have had to  endure the most awful two and a half  weeks of testimony they've had to go  through something no family should ever  have to go through videos were played in  court of their loved ones final moments  propaganda videos of beheadings which  those is beetles those so-called is  beatles who were known by that name they  were given that name by their captives  because of their british accents they  released those videos for propaganda  reasons they were played in court  there were also 10 hostages who were  held alongside those murdered  individuals who also gave evidence  during the course of this trial they  testified about random and regular  beatings waterboarding choking and it  wasn't just  the physical torture that these people  had to endure it was also the  psychological torment that they went  through just to give you one example of  the horror we've heard about over the  past two and a half weeks we were told  that the hostages were forced to fight  each other that they were told to get  dressed in smart clothes given the  impression that they would be released  only to be driven to another prison it  really has been incredibly harrowing for  these families but finally uh they say  they have some sense of justice in that  they  that al shafiel was brought to trial  here in the u.s he's now been found  guilty of all eight charges of which he  was accused
 

